//? Title: Odd-even sort: actual alternating adjacent exchanges
//? Subtitle: Stable identities, phase work and the final zero-swap round
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Follow the actual serial brick-sort producer from a tiny input through the
original seven integers. Canonical comparison and phase histories distinguish
disjoint comparators from parallel execution, and distinguish sorting progress
from the extra rounds used to certify termination.
)

\toc

> Two independent pair patterns, one serial producer

Odd phases compare left slots1,3,...; even phases compare0,2,... . Each
comparison exchanges a strict inversion. Pairs within a phase share no
positions, so they could run concurrently, but this implementation executes them
serially. Equal keys never exchange, hence their original identities remain
ordered.

For a strict adjacent exchange, exactly one inversion disappears:

$$ I(a)=\sum_{i<j}1[a_i>a_j], \qquad I(a_{after})=I(a_{before})-1. $$
\alttext(The inversion count counts out-of-order pairs; one adjacent strict swap reduces that count by one.)

Inversion count cannot become negative, so only finitely many exchanges occur. A
complete odd-plus-even round without swaps tests every adjacent pair without
changing the array; every adjacent inequality is then satisfied and the array is
sorted. This stopping rule includes its final certification round. The
fixed-depth network theorem does not imply that the returned count, including
these extra inspections, is at most n phases.

> A tiny actual phase history

For[3,1,2], the first odd comparison1<2 leaves the input unchanged; the
following even comparison moves1 left. The next odd phase places2 before3. The
diagram and table read the actual snapshots and carried identities.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/odd_even_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/odd_even_sort.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::odd_even_sort_trace({3, 1, 2});
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("input", {0, 0}, std::format("Original\n{}", t.input));
    d.node("even", {7, 0}, std::format("After odd+even\n{}", t.phases[1].values));
    d.node("sorted", {14, 0},
           std::format("After next odd\n{}", t.phases[2].values));
    d.edge("input", "even").edge("even", "sorted");
    std::print("| phase | odd left slots | actual values after | actual swaps |\n| ---: | --- | --- | ---: " "|\n");
    for (auto &s : t.phases)
        std::print("| {} | {} | `{}` | {} |\n", s.ordinal, s.odd, s.values,
                   s.swaps);
    d.save_svg("build/odd_even_tiny.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| phase | odd left slots | actual values after | actual swaps |
| ---: | --- | --- | ---: |
| 0 | true | `[3, 1, 2]` | 0 |
| 1 | false | `[1, 3, 2]` | 1 |
| 2 | true | `[1, 2, 3]` | 1 |
| 3 | false | `[1, 2, 3]` | 0 |
| 4 | true | `[1, 2, 3]` | 0 |
| 5 | false | `[1, 2, 3]` | 0 |
\image(figures/odd_even_tiny.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual first exchanges for three integers, followed by all completed phase states.)
\alttext(An unchanged odd phase precedes the first exchange; final zero-swap phases remain visible in the table.)

> Preserve the original seven-value example

The old report drew eight wires for three rounds while sorting seven values
separately. Here every segment corresponds to an actual comparison of the
original[5,3,8,1,9,2,7], at its real phase and positions. Blue means no
exchange; red means a strict exchange. Separate completed-phase rows show the
resulting arrays. This is the actual adaptive serial execution, not an assertion
that the plotted prefix is a universal fixed sorting network.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/odd_even_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/odd_even_sort.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t =
        dm::algorithms::odd_even_sort_trace(dm::algorithms::odd_even_sort_demo_input());
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    for (auto &c : t.comparisons)
        p.segments({double(c.phase)}, {double(c.left)}, {double(c.phase)},
                   {double(c.left + 1)},
                   c.swapped ? dm::graphics::RGB{220, 38, 38}
                   : dm::graphics::RGB{37, 99, 235}, 2.5);
    p.title("Original seven integers: actual adjacent comparisons").x_label(
        "actual zero-based phase").y_label("zero-based input slot").x_limits(
        -.5, double(t.phases.size()) - .5).y_limits(-.5, 6.5).save_svg(
        "build/odd_even_original.svg");
    std::print("Original: `{}`. Actual result: `{}`. Actual carried IDs: `{}`.\n\n",
               t.input, t.run.output, t.run.original_indices);
    std::print("| phase | actual values | actual comparisons | actual exchanges |\n| ---: | --- | ---: | " "---: |\n");
    for (auto &s : t.phases)
        std::print("| {} | `{}` | {} | {} |\n", s.ordinal, s.values,
                   s.comparisons, s.swaps);
}
```
